    "body": "I think that's doable though. Web IDL types are already defined to be wrappers around various things, e.g. we let [`Promise<T>` be represented by PromiseCapability records](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#js-promise), which is basically a tuple of (actual JS promise object, resolve function, reject function).\r\n\r\nIn general there's a lot of possible improvements to the way `FrozenArray<>` is defined in IDL; see e.g. the discussion in https://github.com/whatwg/webidl/issues/810.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
